{"scenario": "S13", "step": "say", "message": "What documents do I usually need to pay tuition from abroad?", "attachment": false, "reply": "Commonly requested documents for paying tuition from abroad include an official tuition invoice, an admission or enrolment letter, your passport and student visa, and a source-of-funds declaration (such as a bank statement or scholarship letter) [KB: Tuition payment documentation checklist]. Remi also uses an education purpose code for reporting [KB: Purpose-of-payment codes and source of funds]. Requirements vary by country and institution, so always check with your university and bank [KB: Tuition payment documentation checklist].", "cards": ["sources"], "tools": ["search_knowledge"], "provider": "gemini", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "cached": false, "latency_ms": 18392, "actions": []}
